For the stabiliser, closure follows from $(g dot h) x = g (h x) = x$, the identity satisfies $e_G x = x$, and $g x = x$ implies $g^(-1) x = x$. Thus $stab_G(x)$ is a subgroup.

Every $x in X$ lies in its orbit because $x = e x$. If $G x_1 inter G x_2 != emptyset$, write $g_1 x_1 = g_2 x_2$. Then $x_1 = (g_1^(-1) g_2) x_2$, and every $g x_1$ lies in $G x_2$. Hence $G x_1 subset.eq G x_2$, and symmetry gives equality.
